{title: Angel Voices, Ever Singing}
{artist: Francis Pott / Edwin G. Monk}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Opening}
{key: C}
{tempo: 92}
{time: 4/4}
{score: angel-voices-ever-singing.abc}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Open Hymnal score (Angel_Voices_Ever_Singing-Angel_Voices_Monk)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]Angel voices, [F]ever [G]singing,
[Am]Round Thy [C]throne [F]of [G]light,
[C]Angel [Am]harps, [A7]for[D]ever [G]ringing,
[G]Rest not [Am]day [D]or night;__[G]__
[Em]Thousands only [Dm]live to bless Thee,
[C]And con[F]fess [Am]Thee [G]Lord of [C]might.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]Thou who art be[F]yond the [G]farthest
[Am]Mortal [C]eye [F]can [G]scan,
[C]Can it [Am]be [A7]that [D]Thou re[G]gardest
[G]Songs of [Am]sin[D]ful man?__[G]__
[Em]Can we feel that [Dm]Thou art near us
[C]And wilt [F]hear [Am]us? [G]Yea, we [C]can.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]Yea, we know Thy [F]love re[G]joices
[Am]O’er each [C]work [F]of [G]Thine;
[C]Thou didst [Am]ears [A7]and [D]hands and [G]voices
[G]For Thy [Am]praise [D]combine;__[G]__
[Em]Craftsman’s art and [Dm]music’s measure
[C]For Thy [F]plea[Am]sure [G]didst de[C]sign.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[C]Here, great God, to[F]day we [G]offer
[Am]Of Thine [C]own [F]to [G]Thee;
[C]And for [Am]Thine [A7]ac[D]ceptance [G]proffer,
[G]All un[Am]worth[D]ily,__[G]__
[Em]Hearts and minds, and [Dm]hands and voices,
[C]In our [F]choic[Am]est [G]melo[C]dy.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[C]Honor, glory, [F]might and [G]merit,
[Am]Thine shall [C]e[F]ver [G]be,
[C]Father, [Am]Son, [A7]and [D]Holy [G]Spirit,
[G]Blessèd [Am]Tri[D]nity;__[G]__
[Em]Of the best that [Dm]Thou hast given
[C]Earth and [F]Hea[Am]ven [G]render [C]Thee.
{end_of_verse}
